        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0715" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg621"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-08"><hi rendition="#italic">September 8, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 558.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 26th ultimo I had the honor to
                    receive from the minister of state the inclosed rejoinder in the case of
                    Delgado, which I herein send you, with translation. I at once made a prompt and
                    decided response, in which I insisted upon the reclamation as originally made. A
                    copy of such response is herein inclosed for your consideration; and I now await
                    your further instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor</hi>,</signed></closer>











